From e81e1e43ff9575da40ce474d99f333ef4c7f688a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:19:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER (tools 0158): stop goes grey when the program is
 closed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 1003: "我明明把程式關掉了 圖片上停止鈕 卻又還是可以點"
- Checked then: no wb_* and no gdb running on this PC; the moment was not caught,
  so all three possible causes are handled:
  (1) only THIS tree's wb_* light it (tasklist first; their paths asked only when
      one runs -- treeProcs); another folder's wb_serve used to light it;
  (2) every 3 s tick works out state() again and updates when it differs from
      the last shown (a session end out of order / missed: grey within 3 s), and
      one more update 300 ms after a session ends;
  (3) the stop tooltip says why it is lit (stopWhy: building / the debug
      sessions by name / the exes still running).
- Notes: VS Code's own floating debug toolbar hidden on this machine (user
  setting debug.toolBarLocation = hidden; EastSun "這個應該可以不用了 刪掉") --
  the same buttons are on the title bar toolbar.

Tests: run_all 3/3 layers (another folder's wb_serve = grey, this tree's = lit
with its name in the tooltip, gone = grey, a session ended without its event =
grey on the next tick, the session named); real VS Code 156/159 (3 known stale).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
